UC_Reconcile ..> UC_Import : <<include>>

' ---------- Notes ----------
note as N1
  <b>Pay Bill:</b> validates the service amount range
  and the idempotency key.
  The customer sees bill amount, fee, and total before confirming;
  the full total is held.
  Fraud checks enforce the single-payment limit
  (5 - 10,000 EGP), daily limits and velocity rules.
  No answer from a live biller in 10 seconds:
  payment becomes Unknown and funds stay held.
  Biller confirms: held funds are captured.
end note

note as N2
  <b>Retry Unknown Payment:</b> re-queries the biller
  after 1, 5 and 15 minutes.
  The brief does not specify the offsets' anchor; the
  user-approved AQ-15 interpretation (2026-11-25) measures all offsets
  from entry into Unknown. Rationale: deterministic retry times from
  the start of the unresolved state. This records user approval,
  not team/TA approval.
  It never re-sends the payment.
  If all attempts fail to obtain a definitive result,
  payment stays Unknown and funds stay held
  until reconciliation provides evidence.
end note

note as N3
  <b>Reconcile Payment Records:</b> settlement or
  result-file evidence can resolve Unknown payments
  to Completed or Failed.
  Differences are flagged in the report.
  If settlement lists a PayLink Failed payment, flag the mismatch
  for Support review; do not change payment state automatically.
  Late confirmation (callback, retry, settlement)
  triggers capture or release, commission
  and notification as applicable.
end note

note as N4
  <b>Cross-cutting rules:</b> every money movement
  (hold, capture, release, top-up, commission, refund)
  creates a ledger entry.
  Every money movement and admin action
  (billers, fees, limits, account blocks)
  is written to the audit log.
end note

note as N5
  <b>Upgrade Verification Level:</b>
  approval actor is not defined in the brief (AQ-02).
end note

note as N6
  Releasing a failed payment hold is not the same
  as refunding a previously completed payment.
  A definitive failure follows Failed -> Refunded when
  its held funds are released exactly once. FR-27 remains
  optional. The user approved deferring implementation and method,
  amount/eligibility and ledger definition until team/TA resolves
  AQ-07/AQ-12 (2026-11-25); this is not team/TA approval.
  No Completed -> Refunded transition or refund method is approved.
  The completed-payment refund requires a request,
  support review and approval. User-approved AQ-12 proposal, pending
  team/TA confirmation: one authorized Support-role reviewer; audit
  actor, timestamp, outcome, reason, payment/refund identifiers and
  resulting ledger movement; no dual control proposed.
end note

note as N7
  Payment notifications are triggered by payment
  lifecycle events, including late outcomes received
  through callbacks, retries or reconciliation.
  FR-22 requires Completed and Failed outcomes.
  Rejected and separate refund notifications are optional
  proposals and require team approval.
  Notification delivery is independent of payment
  processing.
end note

note as N9
  The brief defines more than 5 payments in 60 seconds
  as the velocity threshold. User-approved AQ-14 interpretation
  (2026-11-25): count payment initiation attempts, including
  attempts later rejected. Rationale: prevent rapid activity evading
  the rule through rejected outcomes. This records user approval only.
  Daily-limit fee/rejected-attempt counting remains open.
end note

note as N8
  Optional NetCo integration is batch-only: Scheduler uploads one
  Payments CSV per day; NetCo returns a Result File the next morning.
  NetCo has no live inquiry use case. Result-file evidence is imported
  for reconciliation and may resolve matching Unknown payments.
end note

@enduml
